From 14709d2ddadb61f4d72f19b2ac4d66624321925b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:36:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: ti: add a machine driver for the Samsung Galaxy Tab 2

The Samsung Galaxy Tab 2 (espresso) tablets have a WM1811 codec on
McBSP3 of the OMAP4430. The codec is the bit and frame clock provider
and needs its FLL set up for each sample rate, which the generic sound
cards can't do: the WM8994 driver has no default SYSCLK source.

Add a machine driver for the HiFi link, based on the Midas WM1811
driver: FLL1 from MCLK1 (26 MHz on these boards, the rate is taken from
the codec's clock) at 256 fs, or 512 fs for 8 and 11.025 kHz, and
regulator supplies for the mic biases. The routes come from the device
tree.

Four things differ from Midas, whose MCLKs are always running:

- MCLK1 is a gated 26 MHz clock here, and the codec takes a reference
  on its SYSCLK source only when AIF1CLK powers up, and drops the one it
  holds for the FLL1 reference while reprogramming FLL1. On a rate
  change the clock then stopped while SYSCLK ran from it, and the codec
  dropped register writes until it came back: FLL1 kept part of its old
  configuration (48 kHz after 44.1 kHz played at 38.8 kHz). The driver
  holds MCLK1 while the codec is biased.
- SYSCLK runs from MCLK1, not from the 32 kHz MCLK2, while FLL1 is
  stopped or reprogrammed, so that it doesn't depend on the TWL6032's
  audio clock, which the codec never enables in that case either.
- FLL1 is only stopped when the bias goes down from PREPARE to
  STANDBY. Going up from OFF, which happens here because nothing keeps
  the codec biased while idle, it reset FLL1 to the default rate after
  hw_params had set it up, and 48 kHz played at 44.1 kHz.
- The codec provides BCLK and LRCLK, but DAPM powers AIF1CLK only for a
  complete path, so a stream with no input or output enabled got no
  clocks and failed with -EIO. AIF1CLK is kept on from hw_params to
  hw_free. A supply alone takes the bias only to STANDBY, never to
  PREPARE, so FLL1 is also stopped on the way to OFF.

Tested on a Galaxy Tab 2 10.1 (GT-P5113): playback at 8, 16, 32, 44.1
and 48 kHz in any order runs at the requested rate (measured from the
hw_ptr), also with no output or input enabled; the speakers and the
internal microphone were checked by ear.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 sound/soc/ti/Kconfig            |  13 +
 sound/soc/ti/Makefile           |   2 +
 sound/soc/ti/samsung-espresso.c | 405 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 420 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sound/soc/ti/samsung-espresso.c

